UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'TWO WRITER-REACH DEFECTS FOUND BY A CODE REVIEW OF BATCH 19, both narrower than they look and both leaving a column no sanctioned verb can fix. (1) journal_name AND publisher ARE NOW CORRECTABLE ONLY ON DOI-BEARING ROWS. Batch 19 added them to db.py _CORRECTABLE so GAP-031 could be discharged, and extended retrieval_log _BIBLIO_FIELDS so the verifier can actually check them -- which restores the invariant _CORRECTABLE header states. BUT correct-source keys its payload BY DOI (db.py: "no DOI, so no payload can be keyed to it"), and amend-source refuses anything in _CORRECTABLE by design. So for a row with no DOI both columns are now unreachable by EVERY sanctioned writer. Derive the exposure rather than quoting it: select count(*) from evidence_sources where coalesce(doi,"")="" -- and note WHICH rows those are, because the bite is precise: a REPORT is the source type whose publisher matters most and the one least likely to carry a DOI. REF-01005, this batch own 1979 HUD report, is exactly that case. THE FIX IS TO KEY THE PAYLOAD BY SOMETHING OTHER THAN A DOI. retrieval_log already resolves locators through several columns for verify_authors (LOCATOR_COLUMNS), and correct-source could take the same route -- url, handle, report_number -- instead of DOI alone. Not attempted in batch 19 because it changes how every correction finds its payload and deserves its own change. (2) PAGE LOCATORS DO NOT DECLARE THEIR NUMBERING, AND THREE ARE IN USE. source_value_extractions.locator_scheme takes the value "page" and nothing says WHICH page: the zero-based index pypdf and pymupdf use, the one-based PDF page a viewer shows, or the number PRINTED on the sheet. For REF-01005 those are 162, 163 and 161 for the same page. Batch 19 wrote 163 on extraction 57 and then, correcting itself, called it "the PDF page index", which is the one thing it is not; extraction 54 from batch 18 carries the same number for the same sheet. A reader holding the physical report is sent to the wrong page, and a reader re-deriving with pypdf is sent to a different wrong page. scripts/research/page_image.py speaks only zero-based indices and says so in its output, which is a start; the schema still does not. CHEAPEST FIX: declare the convention in locator_scheme vocabulary itself -- page_pdf1, page_pdf0, page_printed -- so the column carries the answer instead of a convention nobody wrote down. || CORRECTED 2026-09-28: EXTENDED, batch 21 (session_2026-09-28-research-batch-21-selection), with a concrete instance and a second, related sub-defect this batch found and briefly mis-filed as a new gap (GAP-054, closed as a duplicate of this one by an independent adversarial pass). CONCRETE INSTANCE OF (1): REF-01010 (a DOI-less statutory instrument) needed --pages set at add-source time and was not; amend-source refuses it (bibliographic field) and correct-source refuses it (no DOI to key a payload to) -- exactly item (1)''s mechanism, now for pages/article_number rather than journal_name/publisher. RELATED, NOT YET STATED IN (1): research_batch_dod''s R3 check (clause/section/page citation on regulatory-stratum sources) reads evidence_sources.pages/article_number specifically -- never source_value_extractions.loc_section/loc_subsection/loc_clause, which REF-01010''s own extraction (parameter 3, MOB, 1:12 gradient) DOES carry precisely (loc_section=12, loc_subsection=3, loc_clause=a), byte-verified against the persisted primary PDF (page 15 of 42). So a source can be genuinely, precisely clause-cited at the extraction level and still fail R3 forever, for every DOI-less regulatory/statutory/code source this project ever admits mis-keyed this way -- with no remediation path except getting --pages right on the FIRST add-source call. A THIRD, NARROWER CASE found the same batch: correct-source''s own refusal to write a field the payload states nothing for (''a silence is not a correction'') means even a DOI-HAVING row can end up permanently uncorrectable if a field was originally mis-filed with a value the payload does not carry at all -- REF-01009 stores article-number 237 in  (now duplicated correctly into  too via correct-source, but the wrong  value cannot be nulled by any writer: amend-source refuses it as bibliographic, correct-source refuses to null a field its payload is silent on). WHAT WOULD CLOSE ITEM (1) is unchanged from GAP-043''s own text (key the payload by url/handle/report_number as well as DOI, per LOCATOR_COLUMNS). WHAT WOULD ALSO HELP: either R3 accepting source_value_extractions.loc_* as an alternative satisfying condition, or correct-source gaining an explicit ''set NULL because the payload contradicts the stored value'' mode distinct from its current ''refuse rather than guess'' one. Not remediated this batch; recorded as two reasoned waivers (REF-01010.pages unset, REF-01009.pages left at the wrong value 237 alongside the now-correct article_number=237). || CORRECTED 2026-09-28: CORRECTION TO THE IMMEDIATELY PRECEDING NOTE, same session, self-caught: that note was written via a shell command that put the column names pages and article_number inside backtick characters, which bash interpreted as command substitution ($(pages), $(article_number)) rather than literal text -- both evaluated to empty output, silently deleting those two words from three places in the note. The intended sentence read: "REF-01009 stores article-number 237 in pages (now duplicated correctly into article_number too via correct-source, but the wrong pages value cannot be nulled by any writer: amend-source refuses it as bibliographic, correct-source refuses to null a field its payload is silent on)." The garbled text is left in place above (append-only); this is the correction. || CORRECTED 2026-09-28: EXTENDED AGAIN, batch 22 (session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection), via an independent adversarial pass: this session filed a near-total duplicate of item (1)/its batch-21 extension as a fresh gap (GAP-057), without searching the gaps register first -- the exact rule-5-in-the-gaps-register failure GAP-054 already demonstrates and this file already names as remediated. Closed GAP-057 CLOSED-DUPLICATE; its one genuinely new fact folded in here: the exposure is not limited to REF-01010. Six more DOI-less regulatory sources admitted the same batch (REF-01012 through REF-01017) also omitted --pages at add-source time and are equally unreachable by amend-source (bibliographic, refused) or correct-source (no DOI to key to) -- select count(*) from evidence_sources where tier>=4 and coalesce(pages,'''')='''' and coalesce(article_number,'''')='''' to derive the live count rather than trust this sentence. GAP-057 additionally proposed gating a sanctioned amend-source path for pages/article_number on evidence_type IN (''code'',''standard'') as an alternative to the loc_* fix already proposed here -- recorded as a second candidate fix, not yet attempted.', "updated_at" = '2026-09-28 20:53', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-28-research-batch-22-selection' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-043';

